{"id": "EUVD-2026-96578", "enisaUuid": "82b1f217-c27c-3198-b001-b3ff7b9dec2c", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows any authenticated user to permanently delete data dictionaries via the deletePhysic handler of SysDictController. Low-privileged attackers can send DELETE requests to /sys/dict/deletePhysic/{id} to irreversibly remove active dictionaries and all their items, bypassing the recycle bin.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T12:36:46", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_dict_physic_delete.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysDictController.java#L742-L751", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-dict-deletephysic-id"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108639", "GHSA-w6x3-2fqq-474q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "86ad732d-290d-3d63-8eb3-d374eaced3db", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "434b04ef-35c0-3412-b451-cc4d6c656da7", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}